the mooring does not determine basin-wide length.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Specify source layer and time support, obtain intermediate pathway geometry, and separate branches or dilution thresholds before measuring.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"atlantic-north-equatorial-undercurrent","label":"Separate subsurface sections and historical width scope","audit_file":"research/atlantic-neuc-layer-width-scope-audit.json","summary":"35 Wâ€“23 W editorial reference reach connects separate observational neighborhoods, not a continuous observed axis. Historical month-dated two-degree latitude widths convert to approximately 220 km section spans; transport boxes and seasonal strength are not current dimensions.","source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/pleins_textes_7/b_fdi_51-52/010019670.pdf","source_locator":"Bourles et al. (1999), section 4.8, p. 21163: 35 W NEUC centered at 5 N in February 1993 and April 1996; core near sigma-theta 26.75. Sections 4.6 and 6.1 separate source retroflection from the named current; eastern filament context cites earlier work.","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"atlantic-north-equatorial-undercurrent","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/pleins_textes_7/b_fdi_51-52/010019670.pdf","source_access":"primary_pdf_relevant_sections_read","source_citation":"Bourles, Gouriou and Chuchla (1999), On the circulation in the upper layer of the western equatorial Atlantic, JGR Oceans 104(C9), 21151–21170, doi:10.1029/1999JC900058.","declared_reach_gates":{"upstream":[-35,5],"downstream":[-23,5],"role":"separate_observational_neighborhoods_connected_editorially_not_continuous_observed_axis"},"layer":"Subsurface eastward NEUC context. The central mooring study defines 65–270 m; historical western cores lie near sigma-theta 26.75 kg/m3. These different vertical definitions are not imposed as one uniform layer along the reference line.","observed_period":null,"sampling_context":"Western sections in February 1993 and April 1996; central moorings June 2006–February 2008 and November 2009–January 2018 with 2002–2018 ship sections. Editorial section-to-section geography, not simultaneous observations or an annual/seasonal axis.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_dimension_ranges":null,"rejected_transport_width_transfers":[{"source":"Burmeister et al. (2019), section 2.3","chosen_model_half_width_degrees":2,"observational_offsets_from_core_degrees":[-1.5,1],"reason":"Chosen integration boundaries; not uniform paired current edges."},{"source":"Burmeister et al. (2020), section 4","fixed_transport_box_latitude_degrees":[4.25,5.25],"reason":"Reduced integration box underestimates NEUC transport; not full width."}],"excluded_inferences":["No model 42 W–15 W integration span used as observed whole length.","No 35 W and 23 W records treated as a simultaneous trajectory.","No weak observed seasonal transport cycle converted to seasonal dimensional frames.","No filaments assigned invented eddy identities."],"remaining_gates":["Diagnose a compatible subsurface axis before asserting continuity across the separate section neighborhoods.","Resolve source recirculation, eastern filaments and termination before whole-current length.","Review historical two-degree latitude width with boundary and month-date precision support; no whole width or seasonal range inferred.","Keep mooring transport variability distinct from seasonal length/width geometry."],"historical_width_evidence":{"reported_latitude_span_degrees":2,"reported_center_latitude_degrees":5,"longitude_degrees_east":-35,"observation_months":["1993-02","1996-04"],"layer_context":"Velocity core near sigma-theta 26.75 kg/m3; not fixed-depth width at every level.","source_locator":"Section 4.8, p. 21163; Figs. 3c and 3e","boundary_threshold":null,"numeric_km_inventory_admission":true,"remaining_issue":"Independent extraction review, physical boundary diagnosis and repeated temporal support remain open; exact days unknown.","inventory_status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_ids":["atlantic-neuc-1993-02-angular-section-span","atlantic-neuc-1996-04-angular-section-span"],"approximate_converted_span_km":220,"unrounded_meridional_conversion_km":221.16564339691212}},"source_sha256":"d7ec31e51698fddeba5a3fb9d16ca24243644de0868bd9afa5f994b338d2becd"}]},{"id":"route-decision:atlantic-south-equatorial-countercurrent","entity_id":"current:atlantic-south-equatorial-countercurrent","label":"Atlantic South Equatorial Countercurrent","current_id":"atlantic-south-equatorial-countercurrent","strategy_id":"seasonal_routes","strategy_label":"Construct seasonal routes","construction_status":"reference_path_not_constructed","candidate_count":0,"route_ids":[],"next_action":"Follow research/atlantic-secc-march-1994-section-scope-audit.json: recover time- and layer-compatible longitudinal axes and paired velocity boundaries. Preserve local March 1994 depth-dependent flow and nearby non-detection; do not connect historical sections into a continuous axis or infer annual reversal.","scope":"Ship observations place a weak eastward flow in the 7–9°S belt near 30°W in some seasons, with westward flow in spring 1994. The western survey limit and intermittency prevent a defensible whole-current length.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1175/1520-0485(1998)028%3C1904:TAPOTU%3E2.0.CO;2","source_decision":{"current_id":"atlantic-south-equatorial-countercurrent","name":"Atlantic South Equatorial Countercurrent","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"Ship observations place a weak eastward flow in the 7–9°S belt near 30°W in some seasons, with westward flow in spring 1994. The western survey limit and intermittency prevent a defensible whole-current length.","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1175/1520-0485(1998)028%3C1904:TAPOTU%3E2.0.CO;2","candidate_ids":[],"reference_path_decision":"reference_path_not_constructed","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"eastward upper-ocean countercurrent","route_strategy_id":"seasonal_routes","route_strategy_label":"Construct seasonal routes","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"Ship observations place a weak eastward flow in the 7–9°S belt near 30°W in some seasons, with westward flow in spring 1994. The western survey limit and intermittency prevent a defensible whole-current length.","next_action":"Follow research/atlantic-secc-march-1994-section-scope-audit.json: recover time- and layer-compatible longitudinal axes and paired velocity boundaries. Preserve local March 1994 depth-dependent flow and nearby non-detection; do not connect historical sections into a continuous axis or infer annual reversal.","strategy_next_action":"Choose sourced season, direction and layer; construct each supported seasonal path separately and preserve missing seasons.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"atlantic-south-equatorial-countercurrent","label":"March 1994 current band and vertically separated cores","audit_file":"research/atlantic-secc-march-1994-section-scope-audit.json","summary":"March 1994 flow at 30 W spans a described 6-8 S band, about 220 km meridionally. Two eastward cores are separated by westward flow; this is not fixed-depth full width. Nearby non-detection west of 30 W does not establish basin-wide reversal. Whole-current and annual dimensions remain unresolved.","source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/pleins_textes_7/b_fdi_51-52/010019670.pdf","source_locator":"Section 4.1, printed p. 21156 / PDF index 5; Figure 3a caption p. 21154 / PDF index 3; sections 2 and 2.2.","observed_period":null,"related_current_ids":["atlantic-south-equatorial-undercurrent"]},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"atlantic-south-equatorial-countercurrent","status":"editorial_source_scope_not_scientific_approval","source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/pleins_textes_7/b_fdi_51-52/010019670.pdf","source_access":"Repository PDF sections 2, 2.2 and 4.1 and Figure 3a caption inspected. No figure digitization, raw velocity arrays or cruise reports acquired.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-04","scope":"Local March 1994 CITHER 2 current band at 30 W, 6-8 S. No continuous longitudinal route inferred.","width_record_id":"atlantic-secc-1994-03-described-band-span","source_locator":"Section 4.1, printed p. 21156 / PDF index 5; Figure 3a caption p. 21154 / PDF index 3; sections 2 and 2.2.","observed_month":"1994-03","time_precision":"month","observed_period":null,"cruise_sampling_context":{"start":"1994-01-04","end":"1994-03-21","is_exact_local_section_dates":false},"reported_latitude_limits_degrees":[-8,-6],"reported_section_longitude_degrees_east":-30,"approximate_meridional_band_span_km":220,"unrounded_WGS84_span_km":221.1817565058198,"normalization_center_latitude_degrees":-7,"center_role":"computed_from_reported_limits_for_unit_conversion_only","width_role":"author_described_meridional_band_span_not_fixed_depth_full_width","paired_edges_extracted":false,"fixed_depth_width":false,"depth_context":"Two eastward cores around 40 m and 240 m; westward flow near 7 S around 110 m separates them. Reported flow extends from surface to at least 400 m, not uniformly eastward at every depth.","regional_observation_comparison":"Bourles et al. report nearby Schott et al. non-detection west of 30 W during nearly simultaneous March 1994 sampling. This does not establish basin-wide absence or reversal.","historical_extent_limit":"Historical 14 W/28 W observations and the Stramma (1991) repository abstract suggesting eastward extension to Greenwich do not supply a synchronized source axis. No length calculated by joining them.","secondary_source_access":[{"url":"https://elischolar.library.yale.edu/journal_of_marine_research/2001/","access":"Repository abstract only; downloadable full paper not acquired."}],"naming_rule":"Atlantic SECC and the separately named Atlantic SEUC remain distinct; vertical core structure does not establish alias equivalence.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"seasonal_route_playback_supported":false,"remaining_gates":["Recover exact section occupation days and layer-compatible paired velocity boundaries.","Recover synchronized regional axes and resolve depth-dependent and seasonal continuity.","Independent scientific identity and measurement admission."]},"source_sha256":"774d19e7914c83a9ab13dbd35638dda4fcc7ea07830854576fe2523d613d7578"}]},{"id":"route-decision:atlantic-south-equatorial-undercurrent","entity_id":"current:atlantic-south-equatorial-undercurrent","label":"Atlantic South Equatorial Undercurrent","current_id":"atlantic-south-equatorial-undercurrent","strategy_id":"layer_specific_route","strategy_label":"Construct layer-specific paths","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["atlantic-seuc-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"The 35°W section identifies eastward flow between 2.5°S and 4°S at 200–500 m, with 2.8 Sv mean transport under the study definition. Section transport is not whole-current length.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2002GL016849","source_decision":{"current_id":"atlantic-south-equatorial-undercurrent","name":"Atlantic South Equatorial Undercurrent","existing_length_evidence_status":"section_only","existing_scope":"The 35°W section identifies eastward flow between 2.5°S and 4°S at 200–500 m, with 2.8 Sv mean transport under the study definition. Section transport is not whole-current length.","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2002GL016849","candidate_ids":["atlantic-seuc-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"eastward subsurface jet","route_strategy_id":"layer_specific_route","route_strategy_label":"Construct layer-specific paths","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"The 35°W section identifies eastward flow between 2.5°S and 4°S at 200–500 m, with 2.8 Sv mean transport under the study definition. Section transport is not whole-current length.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Specify source layer and time support, obtain intermediate pathway geometry, and separate branches or dilution thresholds before measuring.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"atlantic-south-equatorial-undercurrent","label":"Subsurface float-study reach versus whole-current extent","audit_file":"research/atlantic-seuc-layer-sampling-scope-audit.json","summary":"35 Wâ€“10 W editorial studied reach in the context of 200 m floats excludes surface drift and recirculation loops. The eastern fate and whole-current dimensions are unresolved; 3â€“6 S sampling band is not width.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2008GL035753","source_locator":"Section 2 [6]â€“[7] and Fig. 1: floats parked at 200 m; 174 ten-day zonal-flow estimates within 3â€“6 S, 35 W to approximately 10 W. Section 4 [9]: mean core around 3 S at 35 W and slightly south of 4 S farther east. Sections 5â€“6: western meanders and unresolved layer-dependent connectivity.","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"atlantic-south-equatorial-undercurrent","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2008GL035753","source_access":"full_primary_publisher_page_read","source_citation":"Fischer, Hormann, Brandt, Schott, Rabe and Funk (2008), South Equatorial Undercurrent in the western to central tropical Atlantic, Geophysical Research Letters 35, doi:10.1029/2008GL035753.","declared_reach_gates":{"upstream":[-35,-3],"downstream":[-10,-4.3],"role":"published_study_longitudes_editorial_core_latitudes_not_whole_current_endpoints"},"layer":"Subsurface eastward flow in the context of floats parked at 200 m. The 200 m level is sampling support, not a uniform core depth or full vertical extent. Ship-section 100–500 m and density-defined transport integrations are separate diagnostics.","observed_period":null,"sampling_context":"Float deployments in 2000–2004 and 2004–2006; ship-section composites span 1990–2008. Editorial geographic reach is not one observed float trajectory, dated axis, annual mean or seasonal series.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_dimension_ranges":null,"source_reported_study_span":{"lower_bound_km":2500,"relation":"greater_than","locator":"Section 2 [7]","role":"float_sampling_domain_span_not_whole_current_length","numeric_canonical_admission":false},"width_scope":"3–6 S describes a float sampling band. Section 4 reports relative widening eastward but no comparable numeric paired-edge width extracted.","excluded_inferences":["No surface westward drift included in subsurface eastward length.","No float recirculation loops or NBUC feeding legs added to main reach.","No transport growth span of 800 km used as whole-current length.","No model boreal-summer strength maximum converted to observed seasonal geometry or length/width margins.","No 1990–2008 section composite dates applied to all float tracks."],"remaining_gates":["Review gates, western meanders and chosen core-latitude smoothing with compatible velocity or trajectory data.","Resolve the eastern rise and fate before whole-current endpoints; 10 W is study truncation.","Separate 200 m float sampling from ship-section depth/density transport definitions and surface drift.","Diagnose paired lateral boundaries before width; 3–6 S is a sampling band, not full-current width."]},"source_sha256":"39056b04353dfc312d3997601d265c3fbe8a3499d873a388da14ca7bfda467b4"}]},{"id":"route-decision:azores-countercurrent","entity_id":"current:azores-countercurrent","label":"Azores Countercurrent","current_id":"azores-countercurrent","strategy_id":"layer_specific_route","strategy_label":"Construct layer-specific paths","construction_status":"reference_path_not_constructed","candidate_count":0,"route_ids":[],"next_action"