ional route","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"A derived minimum north–south span for the coherent shelf-break jet only; not a measured streamline or a published whole-current length. Separation and extension shift over time.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[]},{"id":"route-decision:east-greenland-coastal","entity_id":"current:east-greenland-coastal","label":"East Greenland Coastal Current","current_id":"east-greenland-coastal","strategy_id":"preserve_survey_reach","strategy_label":"Preserve surveyed-reach scope","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"A summer 2004 hydrographic and velocity survey identified this inner-shelf branch along the approximately 1,000 km southeast Greenland shelf south of Denmark Strait. That is a documented regional reach, not a measured whole-current path or a year-round length; the offshore East Greenland Current is distinct.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf","source_decision":{"current_id":"east-greenland-coastal","name":"East Greenland Coastal Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"sampled_reach_only","existing_scope":"A summer 2004 hydrographic and velocity survey identified this inner-shelf branch along the approximately 1,000 km southeast Greenland shelf south of Denmark Strait. That is a documented regional reach, not a measured whole-current path or a year-round length; the offshore East Greenland Current is distinct.","name_source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf","candidate_ids":["east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"low-salinity inner-shelf coastal jet","route_strategy_id":"preserve_survey_reach","route_strategy_label":"Preserve surveyed-reach scope","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"A summer 2004 hydrographic and velocity survey identified this inner-shelf branch along the approximately 1,000 km southeast Greenland shelf south of Denmark Strait. That is a documented regional reach, not a measured whole-current path or a year-round length; the offshore East Greenland Current is distinct.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Reconstruct only the source survey reach first; obtain independent start/end evidence before proposing a broader current route.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"east-greenland-coastal","label":"Coastal studied reach, northern uncertainty and local threshold width","audit_file":"research/east-greenland-coastal-reach-scope-audit.json","summary":"The 66 N to Cape Farewell editorial reach is separate from the source approximately 1000 km shelf survey. Weak northern identification and merging near 63 N limit continuity claims. The 30 km Cape Farewell width uses a 15% inner-jet velocity threshold and cannot buffer this whole route or supply annual margins.","source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf","source_locator":"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), section 3: Cape Farewell and 66 N section geography; section 3.5: weak assumed northern jet near 68 N; sections 8-9: merging near 63 N and approximately 1000 km shelf survey description. Relevant text inspected, no current-axis figure digitized.","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"east-greenland-coastal","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf","source_access":"Accepted manuscript relevant sections 3, 8 and 9 read; source figure screenshot unavailable; no axis digitized. Width sections 2 and 3.1 inspected in previous extraction.","source_citation":"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), The East Greenland Coastal Current: Structure, variability, and forcing, Progress in Oceanography, accepted manuscript.","source_locator":"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), section 3: Cape Farewell and 66 N section geography; section 3.5: weak assumed northern jet near 68 N; sections 8-9: merging near 63 N and approximately 1000 km shelf survey description. Relevant text inspected, no current-axis figure digitized.","scope":"Declared southeast Greenland coastal study-area reach from an OSW offshore gate near 66 N to a Cape Farewell offshore gate near 60 N. Excludes the weak northern 68 N identification, EGC shelfbreak path, Irminger Current, offshore diversions and West Greenland continuation. Not the full EGCC or the source-reported approximately 1000 km surveyed shelf. Near 63 N, the coastal and shelfbreak flows approach or merge; the line does not establish uninterrupted independent coastal flow. The local 30 km Cape Farewell width is not a buffer around this reach.","layer":"Surface-intensified low-salinity inner-shelf jet context from July-August 2004 hydrography and ADCP-referenced geostrophic velocity. No uniform fixed-depth axis diagnosed along this editorial path.","observed_period":null,"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"candidate_file":"research/east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","input_file":"research/east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-input.json","source_shelf_reach_km":1000,"source_shelf_reach_is_current_axis_length":false,"local_width_measurement_id":"east-greenland-coastal-2004-cape-farewell-threshold-section","local_width_km":30,"local_width_velocity_fraction":0.15,"local_width_is_route_buffer":false,"route_approximation":{"reported_approximate_reference_path_km":800,"reported_scenario_range_km":[800,900],"scenario_count":81,"physical_axis_diagnosed":false},"remaining_gates":["Review finer coastline and shelf bathymetry before claiming an inner-shelf current axis.","Resolve northern identification and the 63 N merger before any whole-current extent.","Do not replace the source approximately 1000 km shelf survey description with this shorter editorial reach.","Retain the Cape Farewell 30 km threshold width as a local section; no width buffer or annual footprint inferred."]},"source_sha256":"60349cb57aac6f8602f87b8b88ba3341e39a29cdc603a20aa50d6b9cd92e4ce1"}]},{"id":"route-decision:east-greenland","entity_id":"current:east-greenland","label":"East Greenland Current","current_id":"east-greenland","strategy_id":"source_gated_regional_route","