ion and Cape Farewell. The coast-following route may be longer than the north–south separation; no comparable whole-current centerline length is admitted, so this regional floor is unranked.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[]},{"id":"route-decision:equatorial-countercurrent","entity_id":"current:equatorial-countercurrent","label":"Equatorial Countercurrent","current_id":"equatorial-countercurrent","strategy_id":"split_basin_family","strategy_label":"Split basin families","construction_status":"reference_path_not_constructed","candidate_count":0,"route_ids":[],"next_action":"Measure sourced basin members separately; create any missing child identities before route construction.","scope":"Umbrella label for multiple eastward tropical countercurrents. North and South named families and basin-specific flows require separate boundaries and length estimates.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","source_decision":{"current_id":"equatorial-countercurrent","name":"Equatorial Countercurrent","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"Umbrella label for multiple eastward tropical countercurrents. North and South named families and basin-specific flows require separate boundaries and length estimates.","name_source_url":"https