ning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"ligurian","label":"Ligurian studied segment within Northern Current","audit_file":"research/ligurian-northern-segment-scope-audit.json","summary":"The ledger treats Ligurian Current as a Northern Current segment. This studied reach overlaps the broader current geography; do not add its length to the parent or count it as an independent parallel flow. Surface sampled Genoaâ€“Menton/Nice reach retains editorial gates. Local 15â€“35 km offshore profile band supplies approximately 20 km span; no whole-current or seasonal width inferred.","source_url":"https://mrea.sincem.unibo.it/images/reports/2011_Poulain_Aspects_of_the_surface_circulation.pdf","source_locator":"Poulain et al. (2012), Introduction pp. 261â€“263: NC formation and Italian/French coastal continuation; sections 2.1 and 4, pp. 264â€“266 and 274â€“276: surface sampling, Genoa, Imperia, Mentonâ€“Nice and current structure.","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"ligurian","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://mrea.sincem.unibo.it/images/reports/2011_Poulain_Aspects_of_the_surface_circulation.pdf","source_access":"primary_pdf_relevant_sections_read","source_citation":"Poulain, Gerin, Rixen, Zanasca, Teixeira, Griffa, Molcard, de Marte and Pinardi (2012), Aspects of the surface circulation in the Liguro-Provencal basin and Gulf of Lion as observed by satellite-tracked drifters (2007–2009), Bollettino di Geofisica Teorica ed Applicata 53(2), 261–279, doi:10.4430/bgta0052.","declared_reach_gates":{"upstream":[8.95,44.1],"downstream":[7.35,43.5],"role":"editorial_neighborhood_truncations_not_formal_named_current_endpoints"},"parent_current_id":"northern-mediterranean","parent_scope_note":"The ledger treats Ligurian Current as a Northern Current segment. This studied reach overlaps the broader current geography; do not add its length to the parent or count it as an independent parallel flow.","naming_reference":{"url":"https://www.marineregions.org/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=3357","mrgid":3357,"status":"Proposed standard","endpoint_geometry_present":false,"does_not_establish_osw_segment_convention":true},"layer":"Surface-flow geography in a study combining CODE drifters following the first metre and ARGOSPHERE drifters following the first 10–20 cm with unquantified wind slip. No full-depth or shelf-break axis diagnosed from the editorial route.","sampling_context":"Source drifter sampling is intermittent during May–October 2007 and October 2008–January 2009. The selected reach is editorial geographic context, not one float trajectory, simultaneous observation, annual mean or seasonal path.","observed_period":null,"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_dimension_ranges":null,"additional_width_evidence_pending_definition_review":{"source_locator":"Section 4, p. 274 and Discussion p. 276; Fig. 9","imperia_coast_distance_limit_range_km":[20,30],"interpretation":"Imperia coast-to-limit range remains unresolved as a width metric. Menton–Nice band is now separately extracted as a local approximately 20 km profile-band span, not paired whole-current width or seasonal margin.","numeric_inventory_admission":false},"excluded_inferences":["No basin-wide recirculation loops added to coastal reach length.","No Corsica feeder path or upstream formation location treated as this gate.","No winter/summer parent widths transferred to local segment.","No broad paper sampling 