ifference is 19.5 km. The September 2026 comparison and failed neighbors remain available. Shared inputs, gates and sparse date coverage prevent treating these as independent confirmation, annual extrema, widths or ranked whole-current lengths.","source_url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2023.1156159/full","source_locator":"Sections 2.2, 3.1 and 4.1; local pinned 25 September 2026 experiments","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"loop","as_of":"2026-10-04","status":"editorial_source_and_diagnostic_summary_not_canonical","source_url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2023.1156159/full","source_citation":"Manta et al. (2023), Predicting the Loop Current dynamics combining altimetry and deep flow measurements through the Yucatan Channel, Frontiers in Marine Science 10:1156159, doi:10.3389/fmars.2023.1156159.","source_access":"Full publisher HTML methods and results read. Figures were not digitized. Supplemental numerical Loop Current paths were not acquired.","source_locators":["Sections 2.2, 3.1, 4.1; Figures 1C and 2A captions"],"observed_period":{"start_year":1993,"end_year":2021,"exact_endpoint_days":null},"source_product":"Copernicus DUACS DT-2018 daily 0.25-degree absolute dynamic topography and surface geostrophic velocity","published_metrics":[{"method":"Demeaned 0.17 m sea-level contour connecting Yucatan Channel and Florida Straits","mean_extension_km":1449,"standard_deviation_km":487,"is_confidence_interval":false,"is_length_of_temporal_mean_path":false},{"method":"Maximum-geostrophic-velocity streamline connecting Yucatan Channel and Florida Straits","mean_extension_km":1495,"standard_deviation_km":466,"is_confidence_interval":false,"is_length_of_temporal_mean_path":false}],"method_comparison":{"correlation":0.86,"root_mean_square_difference_km":262},"range_interpretation":"Source describes retracted states below 1000 km and extended phases around 1800–2600 km. These are phase descriptions, not an annual extrema range, confidence interval or width.","diagnostic_file":"research/loop-current-dated-streamline-20260925.json","diagnostic_page":"almanac/loop-current-experiment.html","comparison_diagnostic_file":"research/loop-current-adt-contours-20260925.json","comparison_source_file":"research/gcoos-duacs-loop-20260925.json","comparison_result":"Highest length-weighted mean speed among 31 eligible gateway-connected ADT contours occurs at 0.62 m ADT. Selected path rounds to 2200 km and is 55.9 km shorter than the NOAA trace before display rounding. This is product/method disagreement, not independent observation, uncertainty or a physical range.","diagnostic_observation_date":"2026-09-25","diagnostic_method":"OSW frozen-time velocity integration with strongest northward native-grid seed at an editorial regional gate; distinct from both source contour algorithms","diagnostic_source_product":"NOAA LSA RADS 4.8.1 Experimental daily absolute surface geostrophic velocities; lacks absolute dynamic topography","diagnostic_result":"Nominal gateway-connected path rounds to 2300 km; all four neighboring seed scenarios fail. Integration step changes are small, but no robust range follows from only successful tests.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"rank_eligible":false,"remaining_gates":["Validate gateway placement and section alternatives using geographic and bathymetric evidence","Compatible same-date DUACS ADT acquired through GCOOS; recover original supplemental maximum-velocity algorithm and compare its gateway/method choices","Preserve failed seed outcomes and assess effective resolution and grid masks","Four predeclared dates tested; assess original method/gateway choices and broader repeated-date coverage before describing physical variability or seasonal ranges","Complete scientific and regional