Water spreading around the southwestern Iberian Peninsula, JGR Oceans 107(C10), doi:10.1029/2001JC001007.","declared_reach_gates":{"upstream":[-8.5,36.5],"downstream":[-9.65,38.2],"role":"AMUSE_context_to_editorial_western_slope_truncation_not_whole_current_endpoints"},"layer":"Nonmeddy lower-core Mediterranean Water context, 950–1250 dbar observational selection. Pressure bounds are not converted to uniform depth; vertically separated cores and upstream bottom-trapped density flow remain distinct.","observed_period":null,"sampling_context":"AMUSE floats deployed May 1993–March 1994 and tracked for up to 11 months, with May 1993 hydrography and augmented Iberian observations. Selected path is editorial geography, not one dated float trajectory, annual mean or seasonal axis.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_dimension_ranges":null,"width_scope":"30 km core-to-offshore zero crossing and 10 km geostrophic survey band have different boundaries and support; not a seasonal pair.","additional_width_evidence_pending_definition_review":{"source_locator":"Results 3.2 [22]","reported_lower_bound_km":50,"feature":"Mean northward-flow band in western slope Region 2, 0.04–0.06 m/s; source says at least 50 km, not a paired-edge whole-current width.","numeric_inventory_admission":false},"excluded_inferences":["No upstream gravity-current route silently joined to lower core.","No salt-tongue geometry equated with current axis.","No meddy float loops counted in boundary-current length.","No float launch window treated as observation end dates."],"remaining_gates":["Review launch neighborhood, cape detour and 38.2 N longitude against finer bathymetry and observational support.","Diagnose a depth/time-compatible current axis before physical length or seasonal bounds.","Resolve western-slope branch loss and farther-north continuity before whole-current endpoints.","Keep 30 km one-sided ensemble span and 10 km survey band separate; no seasonal 10–30 km width range or buffered footprint."]},"source_sha256":"4f71a744f40022a2de29b70f70d0ddc4b6eb789762b696b28f4cb23e71e5a84f"}]},{"id":"route-decision:mindanao-current","entity_id":"current:mindanao-current","label":"Mindanao Current","current_id":"mindanao-current","strategy_id":"source_gated_regional_route","strategy_label":"Establish a sourced regional route","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["mindanao-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"The source describes flow southward along the Philippine Islands and supply to the Indonesian Throughflow, North Equatorial Countercurrent, and Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent. It gives no whole-current alongflow length or fixed endpoint gates.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2011JC007477","source_decision":{"current_id":"mindanao-current","name":"Mindanao Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"The source describes flow southward along the Philippine Islands and supply to the Indonesian Throughflow, North Equatorial Countercurrent, and Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent. It gives no whole-current alongflow length or fixed endpoint gates.","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2011JC007477","candidate_ids":["mindanao-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"southward low-latitude western boundary current","route_strategy_id":"source_gated_regional_route","route_strategy_label":"Establish a sourced regional route","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"The source describes flow southward along the Philippine Islands and supply to the Indonesian Throughflow, North Equatorial Countercurrent, and Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent. It gives no whole-current alongflow length or fixed endpoint gates.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[]},{"id":"route-decision:monsoon","entity_id":"current:monsoon","label":"Monsoon Current","current_id":"monsoon","strategy_id":"seasonal_routes","strategy_label":"Construct seasonal routes","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":2,"route_ids":["monsoon-summer-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate","monsoon-winter-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"Seasonal reversal changes the path and direction.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","source_decision":{"current_id":"monsoon","name":"Monsoon Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"Seasonal reversal changes the path and direction.","name_source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","candidate_ids":["monsoon-summer-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate","monsoon-winter-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"seasonal current","route_strategy_id":"seasonal_routes","route_strategy_label":"Construct seasonal routes","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"Seasonal reversal changes the path and direction.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Choose sourced season, direction and layer; construct each supported seasonal path separately and preserve missing seasons.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"monsoon","label":"Seasonal reversal, shallow layers and counterflows","audit_file":"research/monsoon-sri-lanka-seasonal-layer-scope-audit.json","summary":"South of Sri Lanka, the source defines eastward June–September SMC and westward November–February NMC phases. The 77–83 E reference drawings use editorial gates and bends. Shallow surface flow, near-coastal opposite flow, equatorial jets and undercurrents remain separate. Latitude spans are not current widths; transition geometry and annual dimensions remain unresolved.","source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf","source_locator":"Section 5.1.5, printed pp. 63–65 / PDF indices 62–64; Figure 48 caption distinguishes August 1993 and January 1991 sections.","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"monsoon","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf","source_citation":"Schott and McCreary (2001), The monsoon circulation of the Indian Ocean, Progress in Oceanography 51, 1–123, doi:10.1016/S0079-6611(01)00083-0.","source_locator":"Section 5.1.5, printed pp. 63–65 / PDF indices 62–64; Figure 48 caption distinguishes August 1993 and January 1991 sections.","source_access":"Original review PDF section 5.1.5 and Figure 48 caption read. Schott et al. (1994) publisher-indexed abstract read; direct full article retrieval failed. No figure, model curve or velocity field digitized.","scope":"Two declared 77–83 E Sri Lanka regional seasonal reaches under the existing Monsoon Current name; no upstream/downstream whole-current endpoints determined.","layer":"Near-surface regional reference context; historical local profiles are shallow and depth dependent. Subsurface counterflows and equatorial jets remain separate.","time_convention":"Boreal source labels, June–September SMC and November–February NMC. Transition geometry is missing; reported persistence beyond February is not forced into the nominal winter calendar.","observed_period":null,"seasonal_phases":[{"label":"Southwest Monsoon Current","calendar_months":[6,7,8,9],"flow_direction":"eastward","source_label_role":"seasonal_phase_under_existing_name_not_new_canonical_current"},{"label":"Northeast Monsoon Current","calendar_months":[11,12,1,2],"flow_direction":"westward","source_label_role":"seasonal_phase_under_existing_name_not_new_canonical_current"}],"local_section_context":{"longitude_east":80.5,"summer_section_period":"1993-08","winter_section_period":"1991-01","summer_local_core_latitude_north":4,"near_coast_counterflow_band_latitude_north":[5.5,6],"section_context_defines_whole_route":false,"source_reported_layer_context":"Review describes a shallow summer flow and roughly 120 m January 1991 winter penetration locally; neither fixes an axis depth across the route.","latitude_bands_are_current_widths":false},"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"physical_axis_diagnosed":false,"monthly_observed_geometry_established":false,"route_construction_status":"two_editorial_seasonal_regional_candidates_not_canonical","route_approximations":[{"phase":"summer","candidate_file":"research/monsoon-summer-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate.json","input_file":"research/monsoon-summer-sri-lanka-reference-path-input.json","approximate_reference_path_km":800,"editorial_scenario_range_km":[700,900],"scenario_count":27,"observed_seasonal_length":false},{"phase":"winter","candidate_file":"research/monsoon-winter-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate.json","input_file":"research/monsoon-winter-sri-lanka-reference-path-input.json","approximate_reference_path_km":700,"editorial_scenario_range_km":[600,900],"scenario_count":27,"observed_seasonal_length":false}],"supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/pdf/10.1029/94JC02216","citation":"Schott, Reppin, Fischer and Quadfasel (1994), Currents and transports of the Monsoon Current south of Sri Lanka.","locator":"Publisher-indexed abstract; direct full article unavailable.","supports":"Local mooring/ship observations distinguish shallow surface flow, seasonal reversal and nearby opposite flow. Transport integration support is not a longitudinal route or complete transverse width."}],"remaining_gates":["Review seasonal velocity axes, fixed regional gates and connecting coordinates.","Resolve Arabian Sea sources, Bay of Bengal continuation and seasonal branches independently before whole-current length.","Recover March–May/October geometry; nominal months are conventions, not instantaneous reversal dates.","Recover matching transverse velocity boundaries; section integration bands cannot become whole-current width.","Review seasonal phase identity and aliases without double-counting the umbrella current."]},"source_sha256":"0887d278f8996560f932453aef28bdafa04882b3e150731b36e179eb11b033ce"}]},{"id":"route-decision:new-guinea-coastal-current","entity_id":"current:new-guinea-coastal-current","label":"New Guinea Coastal Current","current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-current","strategy_id":"seasonal_routes","strategy_label":"Construct seasonal routes","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["new-guinea-coastal-surface-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"Three years of moorings distinguish this upper-100 m current from the deeper New Guinea Coastal Undercurrent: it flows southeastward in boreal winter and northwestward in boreal summer. The observations do not define a whole-current alongflow length.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2020JC016242","source_decision":{"current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-current","name":"New Guinea Coastal Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"Three years of moorings distinguish this upper-100 m current from the deeper New Guinea Coastal Undercurrent: it flows southeastward in boreal winter and northwestward in boreal summer. The observations do not define a whole-current alongflow length.","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2020JC016242","candidate_ids":["new-guinea-coastal-surface-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"seasonally reversing surface western boundary current","route_strategy_id":"seasonal_routes","route_strategy_label":"Construct seasonal routes","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"Three years of moorings distinguish this upper-100 m current from the deeper New Guinea Coastal Undercurrent: it flows southeastward in boreal winter and northwestward in boreal summer. The observations do not define a whole-current alongflow length.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Choose sourced season, direction and layer; construct each supported seasonal path separately and preserve missing seasons.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-current","label":"Local seasonal direction and El Niño exception","audit_file":"research/new-guinea-coastal-current-seasonal-direction-scope-audit.json","summary":"Local upper-ocean direction composite reverses southeastward November–April to northwestward May–October. Three-cycle sampling, gaps and El Niño exceptions limit annual interpretation. Direction symbols are not current axes or measured seasonal lengths/widths.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2020JC016242","source_locator":"Data and Method, sections 3.2–3.3 / Figures 4 and 9 captions","observed_period":null,"related_current_ids":["new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent"]},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-seasonal-direction-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-current","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_summary_not_canonical","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2020JC016242","source_citation":"Zhang et al. (2020), Seasonal and Interannual Variability of the Currents off the New Guinea Coast From Mooring Measurements, doi:10.1029/2020JC016242.","source_access":"Publisher abstract, Introduction, Data and Method, sections 3.1–3.3 and figure captions read. No figure, velocity field or axis digitized.","observed_period":{"start":"2015-11","end":"2018-12"},"time_precision":"month","scope":"Local alongshore direction at the 141.4 E, 1.7 S mooring; monthly composite of three cycles, with interannual contamination and instrument gaps. Not a whole-current monthly path.","sampling_note":"Data above 30 m removed; upper-400 m instrument outage July 2016–March 2017. Monthly averages; three cycles provide limited independence.","interpretation":"November–April southeastward and May–October northwestward describe the short-record composite. In the 2015/2016 El Niño interval the eastward NGCC disappears as NGCUC shoals. Exception is selectable separately and excluded from seasonal playback.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"route_construction_status":"not_constructed","phases":[{"current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-current","geometry_role":"local_direction_symbol_not_current_axis","site_lon_lat":[141.4,-1.7],"layer":"Upper-100 m NGCC context; ADCP measurements above 30 m excluded. No uniform layer assigned along a route.","length_km":null,"width_km":null,"route_coordinates":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2020JC016242","id":"ngcc-november-april","phase_label":"November–April · three-cycle composite","flow_direction":"southeastward","calendar_months":[11,12,1,2,3,4],"phase_kind":"seasonal_direction_composite","playback_eligible":true,"observed_period":{"start":"2015-11","end":"2018-12"},"source_locator":"Section 3.2 / Figure 4 caption"},{"current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-current","geometry_role":"local_direction_symbol_not_current_axis","site_lon_lat":[141.4,-1.7],"layer":"Upper-100 m NGCC context; ADCP measurements above 30 m excluded. No uniform layer assigned along a route.","length_km":null,"width_km":null,"route_coordinates":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2020JC016242","id":"ngcc-may-october","phase_label":"May–October · three-cycle composite","flow_direction":"northwestward","calendar_months":[5,6,7,8,9,10],"phase_kind":"seasonal_direction_composite","playback_eligible":true,"observed_period":{"start":"2015-11","end":"2018-12"},"source_locator":"Section 3.2 / Figure 4 caption"},{"current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-current","geometry_role":"local_direction_symbol_not_current_axis","site_lon_lat":[141.4,-1.7],"layer":"Upper-100 m NGCC context; ADCP measurements above 30 m excluded. No uniform layer assigned along a route.","length_km":null,"width_km":null,"route_coordinates":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2020JC016242","id":"ngcc-el-nino-2015-2016","phase_label":"2015/2016 El Niño exception","flow_direction":"southeastward NGCC absent; northwestward undercurrent shoals","calendar_months":null,"phase_kind":"event_exception","playback_eligible":false,"observed_period":{"start":"2015-11","end":"2016-06"},"source_locator":"Section 3.3 / Figure 9 caption"}],"remaining_gates":["Recover cross-flow boundaries and alongshore axes before seasonal dimensions.","Resolve calendar dependence across ENSO states and a longer record.","Keep NGCC, NGCUC and newly named intermediate flow distinct."]},"source_sha256":"8b5fc2d62a5a7c777b69106aa7875260d52bbdff9a2059fbe06d6a1d364652fc"}]},{"id":"route-decision:new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent","entity_id":"current:new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent","label":"New Guinea Coastal Undercurrent","current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent","strategy_id":"layer_specific_route","strategy_label":"Construct layer-specific paths","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"The source describes northwestward flow along Papua New Guinea and through Vitiaz Strait into the Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent source region. It gives no comparable whole-current centerline length.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2011JC007477","source_decision":{"current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent","name":"New Guinea Coastal Undercurrent","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"The source describes northwestward flow along Papua New Guinea and through Vitiaz Strait into the Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent source region. It gives no comparable whole-current centerline length.","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2011JC007477","candidate_ids":["new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"northwestward subsurface western boundary current","route_strategy_id":"layer_specific_route","route_strategy_label":"Construct layer-specific paths","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"The source describes northwestward flow along Papua New Guinea and through Vitiaz Strait into the Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent source region. It gives no comparable whole-current centerline length.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Specify source layer and time support, obtain intermediate pathway geometry, and separate branches or dilution thresholds before measuring.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent","label":"Subsurface PNG reach, mooring support and boreal source seasons","audit_file":"research/new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent-layer-season-scope-audit.json","summary":"Northern PNG editorial reach is separate from the seasonally reversing surface New Guinea Coastal Current. The source uses boreal labels south of the equator; its local 150–250 m undercurrent core and ENSO shoaling do not provide annual path or width geometry. Vitiaz passage, other branches and downstream EUC lengths are excluded.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2002JC001611","source_locator":"Ueki et al. (2003), Introduction [2]â€“[7]: separate surface and thermocline flows, northern PNG coast and gateway relations; Data [8]: 142 E moorings; Results 3.1 [17]â€“[18]: local 150â€“250 m core and El Nino shoaling. Relevant text inspected; no current axis digitized.","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2002JC001611","source_citation":"Ueki, Kashino and Kuroda (2003), Observation of current variations off the New Guinea coast including the 1997â€“1998 El Nino period and their relationship with Sverdrup transport, Journal of Geophysical Research: Oceans, doi:10.1029/2002JC001611.","source_locator":"Ueki et al. (2003), Introduction [2]â€“[7]: separate surface and thermocline flows, northern PNG coast and gateway relations; Data [8]: 142 E moorings; Results 3.1 [17]â€“[18]: local 150â€“250 m core and El Nino shoaling. Relevant text inspected; no current axis digitized.","source_access":"Relevant publisher introduction, Data [8]–[10], Table 1 and Results [17]–[18] read; figures and ADCP fields not digitized.","scope":"Declared north-Papua New Guinea regional reach from an OSW offshore Vitiaz-downstream approach gate near 147 E, 4.5 S to the 142 E, 2.5 S mooring neighborhood. Excludes passage through Vitiaz Strait itself, upstream Solomon Sea coastal branches, New Britain and St Georges branches, and the cross-equatorial EUC connection. Gates do not establish whole-current origin or termination.","layer":"Subsurface thermocline flow. Ueki et al. report a local northwestward core generally at 150â€“250 m near the moorings; the core shoals during El Nino. This local depth support is not a fixed-depth axis assigned along the entire editorial reach. Surface New Guinea Coastal Current remains a separate identity.","observed_period":null,"source_mooring_locations_lon_lat":[[142,-2],[142,-2.5]],"source_mooring_locations_are_route_endpoints":false,"source_local_core_depth_context_m":[150,250],"source_local_core_is_uniform_route_layer":false,"source_season_convention":{"label_basis":"boreal","role":"source_observation_labels_only","months_by_label":{"winter":[1,2,3],"summer":[7,8,9],"fall":[10,11,12]},"source_locator":"Ueki et al. (2003), Data [10], Table 1 footnote: source defines Northern Hemisphere season labels and month windows.","supports_annual_route_geometry":false},"source_seasonality_scope":"Local undercurrent remains northwestward with boreal summer intensification in the record, with ENSO-related shoaling. Surface current reversal is a separate current. No annual geometry series extracted.","source_sampling_context":"Two upward-looking 150-kHz ADCP moorings; changing sampled depth bounds approximately 30–50 to 200–330 m, subsampled at 10 m intervals. Not uniform vertical support along route.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"route_construction_status":"editorial_candidate_constructed_not_canonical","candidate_file":"research/new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate.json","input_file":"research/new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-input.json","route_approximation":{"reported_approximate_reference_path_km":600,"reported_scenario_range_km":[500,700],"scenario_count":81,"physical_axis_diagnosed":false},"remaining_gates":["Review finer coastline and bathymetry before claiming a subsurface coastal axis.","Resolve upstream branch convention, gateway passages and downstream equatorial connection separately.","Local 150â€“250 m core cannot establish a uniform fixed-depth path, and surface monsoon reversal cannot be transferred to the undercurrent.","Obtain comparable dated geometry or cross-flow sections before annual length/width margins."]},"source_sha256":"44153b6d41d13880780d4583255e276a9f69278db88ff2204caead1cb5abf22e"}]},{"id":"route-decision:new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent","entity_id":"current:new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent","label":"New Ireland Coastal Undercurrent","current_id":"new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent","strategy_id":"layer_specific_route","strategy_label":"Construct layer-specific paths","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"The source describes flow along New Ireland's eastern coast, with branches joining the New Guinea Coastal Undercurrent or retroflecting toward the Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent. It gives no whole-current length.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2011JC007477","source_decision":{"current_id":"new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent","name":"New Ireland Coastal Undercurrent","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"The source describes flow along New Ireland's eastern coast, with branches joining the New Guinea Coastal Undercurrent or retroflecting toward the Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent. It gives no whole-current length.","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2011JC007477","candidate_ids":["new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"subsurface island boundary current","route_strategy_id":"layer_specific_route","route_strategy_label":"Construct layer-specific paths","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"The source describes flow along New Ireland's eastern coast, with branches joining the New Guinea Coastal Undercurrent or retroflecting toward the Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent. It gives no whole-current length.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Specify source layer and time support, obtain intermediate pathway geometry, and separate branches or dilution thresholds before measuring.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent","label":"Subsurface coastal reach versus modeled branching pathways","audit_file":"research/new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent-branch-model-scope-audit.json","summary":"East New Ireland editorial coastal reach excludes downstream retroflection, Bismarck continuation and EUC length. Subsurface geography is not a NASA surface observation; the source model closes St Georges Channel at its resolution. Exact layer, dated geometry, whole-current width and annual margins remain unresolved.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2011JC007477","source_locator":"Grenier et al. (2011), Introduction [5] and Figure 1 caption: NICU along eastern New Ireland and separate NGCU/SICU; section 2.1 [12]â€“[15]: 0.25-degree model and gateway limitations; section 3.2 [22] and coastal pathway discussion. Relevant text read; no source axis digitized.","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2011JC007477","source_citation":"Grenier et al. (2011), From the western boundary currents to the Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent: Modeled pathways and water mass evolutions, Journal of Geophysical Research: Oceans 116, doi:10.1029/2011JC007477.","source_locator":"Grenier et al. (2011), Introduction [5] and Figure 1 caption: NICU along eastern New Ireland and separate NGCU/SICU; section 2.1 [12]â€“[15]: 0.25-degree model and gateway limitations; section 3.2 [22] and coastal pathway discussion. Relevant text read; no source axis digitized.","source_access":"Publisher relevant introduction, model description/validation and pathway discussion read; no full-article read or source geometry digitization claimed.","scope":"Declared regional east-coast New Ireland reach from an OSW southeastern offshore gate near 153.6 E, 4.5 S to an OSW northern offshore gate near 150.9 E, 2.2 S. Excludes Solomon Strait inflow across the basin, New Britain and St Georges branches, Bismarck Sea westward continuation, retroflection and downstream EUC route. Gates are editorial truncations, not whole-current origin or termination.","layer":"Subsurface thermocline boundary-current geography. Grenier et al. discuss density-dependent modeled pathways; no single fixed-depth axis or whole-depth current footprint extracted for this coastal reach.","observed_period":null,"source_model":"ORCA025-G70, 0.25-degree eddy-permitting OGCM, 46 vertical levels; five-day mean outputs.","source_model_period_context":{"simulation_start_year":1958,"simulation_end_year":2004,"analysis_end_year":2001,"is_dated_current_geometry":false},"source_model_limitations":["St Georges Channel closed by model resolution, not physically absent.","NGCU core poorly simulated at the PNG mooring; coastal position sensitivity noted.","The model source pathways are not a measured NICU centerline."],"other_source_access":[{"url":"https://journals.ametsoc.org/view/journals/phoc/46/10/jpo-d-16-0107.1.xml","access":"Publisher page returned internal retrieval error; no additional numeric extraction.","role":"Future observed-pathway corroboration"}],"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"route_construction_status":"editorial_candidate_constructed_not_canonical","candidate_file":"research/new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate.json","input_file":"research/new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-input.json","route_approximation":{"reported_approximate_reference_path_km":400,"reported_scenario_range_km":[300,500],"scenario_count":81,"physical_axis_diagnosed":false,"source_particle_paths_digitized":false},"remaining_gates":["Review finer island coastline and bathymetry before claiming a subsurface coastal axis.","Resolve northern branching and southern entrance convention before whole-current extent.","Source model closes St Georges Channel at this resolution; do not infer that channel is physically absent.","Do not transfer source EUC dimensions or gateway section dimensions to the NICU."]},"source